<title>FRANCE: Lagardere stock falls eight pct in Paris.</title>
<headline>Lagardere stock falls eight pct in Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lagardere were the biggest losers on the CAC-40 index on Monday morning after a Socialist-led parliamentary victory raised doubts about the privatisation of defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>Shares in Lagardere, the publishing-to-missiles conglomerate tipped to acquire the state's 58 percent stake in Thomson-CSF, were down 8.01 percent at 156.20. Thomson-CSF shares were off 7.54 percent at 152.10. The CAC-40 index was 3.3 percent lower.</p>
</text>
